# Build specs

- Read build-specs/README.md before writing or changing a spec.
- A new spec is a copy of build-specs/TEMPLATE.md named YYYY-MM-DD-short-kebab-name.md.
  Never edit TEMPLATE.md.
- Cursor writes specs and leaves them at `status: draft`. Cursor never sets `reviewed`,
  `in-progress`, or `built`. Claude does the review by following build-specs/REVIEW.md.
- Never edit a spec whose status is `reviewed`, `in-progress`, or `built`. If it needs to
  change, tell Nick and let the review loop handle it, or write a new spec.
- Always pull main before touching build-specs/. Work on a new branch, never on a branch
  that has already been merged.
- When a spec is added, add its row to the index in build-specs/README.md.
- No secrets, real email addresses, or tokens in a spec.
